CampusLoop 3.0 — Complete University Marketplace & Student Lifestyle Platform

PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a complete, responsive, functional university marketplace and student lifestyle web application called CampusLoop.

CampusLoop is designed specifically for university students. It should help students buy and sell second-hand items, borrow useful belongings, find items they need, compare prices, communicate safely, manage their spending, and participate in a friendly campus community.

The application should feel like a real student startup product, not a generic AI-generated dashboard or a static landing page.

I am a beginner programmer. Generate clean, understandable, well-organized code with clear component names and a simple project structure.

Use React and TypeScript if supported by the project environment.

IMPORTANT:

* Build a working frontend prototype, not just a visual mockup.
* Preserve and improve all existing CampusLoop functionality.
* Do not remove existing features when adding new ones.
* Do not add payment processing or unnecessary AI features.
* Do not pretend that authentication, cloud storage, live pricing, or real-time multi-user functionality works unless actually implemented.
* Use realistic sample data and clearly label simulated information.
* Run the application and test the available browser preview if the environment supports it.
* Fix build errors and obvious runtime errors before finishing.

